ite named above passes with no edit to any assertion' — a symbol removal breaks resolution before any assertion runs."],"finding":"The named pinning suite tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py binds push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths directly (lines 286, 358, 372) and monkeypatches it (line 311), but the plan says push_recovery 'drops its private mover' and lists delegating adapters ONLY for sync — leaving no adapter for _quarantine_untracked_paths in push_recovery. Dropping the symbol breaks these tests at binding/monkeypatch time, not merely at an assertion, contradicting the AC that this suite passes with no assertion edits.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2647720de9b8c501","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('push_recovery drops its private mover') / Testing (pinning list) / AC3 (no pinned behaviour changes)","norm_id":"n1f4f2a0868454d5b","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running test_push_recovery_untracked.py after _quarantine_untracked_paths is removed from push_recovery — the direct calls and monkeypatch.setattr raise AttributeError."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths(core, base_path, paths) as a delegating adapter over merge_recovery.quarantine_untracked (with core._git resolved at call time), mirroring the sync adapter treatment, so the pinning test's direct calls and monkeypatch.setattr keep working.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either retain push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths as a thin delegating adapter with its existing (core, base_path, paths) shape, or explicitly account in Scope/Testing for updating its call sites and monkeypatch site in tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py (lines 286, 311, 358, 372) — derived from find_referencing_symbols plus a string grep for the setattr name.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach: 'push_recovery drops its private mover and its import from sync, delegating through merge_recovery with core._git resolved at call time.'","Plan Testing: 'Pinning, to pass with NO assertion edits: ... tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py'","tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py:286 `moved = push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths(push, str(tracker), [_COLLIDE_PATH, _TRACKED_LOCAL])`","tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py:311 `monkeypatch.setattr(push_recovery, \"_quarantine_untracked_paths\", fake_move)`","tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py:358,372 direct calls to `push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths(core, str(tmp_path), ...)`","Contrast: the plan DOES enumerate sync-side retained names (_quarantine_untracked, _restore_local_changes, _untracked_overwrite_paths, _local_change_paths, _quarantine_dir_under) but names no push_recovery-side retained symbol."],"finding":"The plan removes push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths ('drops its private mover') but omits it from the adapter-retention inventory, unlike the parallel sync-side name list. The pinning suite test_push_recovery_untracked.py binds this exact symbol as a live name: direct calls at lines 286, 358, 372 (signature (core, base_path, paths)) and a monkeypatch.setattr(push_recovery, \"_quarantine_untracked_paths\", fake_move) at line 311. The plan requires that suite to pass with no assertion edits, yet removing the symbol breaks these non-assertion call/patch sites.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4d4a7be37265dc0a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: \"push_recovery drops its private mover and its import from sync, delegating through merge_recovery\"; Testing: pinning list naming test_push_recovery_untracked.py","norm_id":"n7fe432dae2cf4acf","priority":0.9,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["test_push_recovery_untracked.py:286 (test_quarantine_refuses_tracked_path) calls push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths directly — AttributeError after removal, a pinning-suite failure not fixable by an assertion edit.","test_push_recovery_untracked.py:311 monkeypatch.setattr(push_recovery, \"_quarantine_untracked_paths\", fake_move) — a string-keyed patch site the LSP will not surface; setattr on a missing attribute breaks test_quarantine_aborts_merge_before_moving_files.","test_push_recovery_untracked.py:358 and :372 (unresolvable common-dir / vanished-path tests) both invoke the symbol directly and fail if it is dropped without a same-signature adapter."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths(core, base_path, paths) as a thin adapter delegating to merge_recovery.quarantine_untracked (binding core._git at call time), mirroring the sync-side adapter treatment, so the pinning suite's calls and monkeypatch.setattr keep resolving.","tier":"LLM","validity":